The local prior for 2022 still matters here: Mexico shows no state-based or internationalized conflict events or fatalities, and the usable 2B record is almost entirely diplomatic. That makes this a limited-exposure chapter, with the key question being whether AMLO and his foreign-policy team used the available room for de-escalation, lawful peace, and humanitarian restraint.

**New Evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Situation along Russian Federation-Ukraine Border Can Only Be Resolved through Diplomacy, Political Affairs Chief Tells Security Council","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-01-31","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14783.doc.htm","claim":"Mexico said the key principles were the prohibition of the threat or use of force, non-intervention, and peaceful settlement of disputes; it said there was no military solution and that diplomatic paths had not been exhausted.","locator":"Mexico statement in meeting coverage","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous UN Security Council record of Mexico's official statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit, just before the invasion escalated into full-scale war.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional Mexican foreign-policy position under AMLO; attributed to Mexico's UN delegation rather than a personal directive from AMLO.","contrary_evidence":["Mexico initially framed the issue cautiously and did not endorse immediate coercive measures beyond diplomacy.","This is crisis diplomacy, not proof of unique presidential initiative."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico takes part in the UN Human Rights Council High-Level Segment","publisher":"Secretaría de Relaciones Exteriores","publication_date":"2022-03-01","url":"https://www.gob.mx/sre/prensa/mexico-takes-part-in-the-un-human-rights-council-high-level-segment","claim":"Mexico condemned the invasion of Ukraine, called for stronger multilateral organizations, and said the situation required states to reaffirm peace and respect for human rights.","locator":"Press release bullet points and opening paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary foreign-ministry release dated during the opening phase of the war.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Government of Mexico under AMLO; not a direct personal statement by AMLO.","contrary_evidence":["This is a broad normative statement, not an operational peace action.","It does not resolve the question of whether later Mexican diplomacy was effective."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico participates in UN Human Rights Council urgent debate on Ukraine","publisher":"Secretaría de Relaciones Exteriores","publication_date":"2022-03-03","url":"https://www.gob.mx/sre/prensa/mexico-participates-in-un-human-rights-council-urgent-debate-on-ukraine?idiom=en","claim":"Mexico said it voted in favor of the urgent debate on Ukraine, condemned the invasion and human-rights violations, and said it would keep urging parties to keep diplomatic channels open for a peaceful resolution.","locator":"Press release summary and opening paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary release with explicit vote and stated rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Mexican state action under AMLO; the statement is made by an undersecretary, so attribution is institutional rather than personal.","contrary_evidence":["A vote for debate is not the same as a negotiated settlement.","It does not show AMLO personally driving the action."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexican Air Force plane arrives in Mexico with 81 passengers evacuated from Ukraine: Ebrard","publisher":"Secretaría de Relaciones Exteriores","publication_date":"2022-03-04","url":"https://www.gob.mx/sre/articulos/mexican-air-force-plane-arrives-in-mexico-with-81-passengers-evacuated-from-ukraine-ebrard-296088","claim":"Mexico strongly condemned the invasion, evacuated people from Ukraine by air force aircraft, and said it would not apply unilateral sanctions against another country.","locator":"Opening bullet points and first paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government release tied to a dated evacuation operation and policy statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Government action under AMLO; the evacuation was instructed by the president, but the sanctions line is a government policy position rather than a uniquely personal act.","contrary_evidence":["Refusing unilateral sanctions is restraint, but it can also be read as hedging rather than active peace-making.","This does not prove deeper conflict-resolution leverage."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.6","2B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Fails to Adopt Text Demanding Civilian Protection, Unhindered Humanitarian Access in Ukraine, as 13 Members Abstain","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-03-23","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14838.doc.htm","claim":"Mexico said it and France had negotiated a humanitarian draft in good faith; Mexico explained it abstained on the Russian alternative because it omitted Article 2.4 of the UN Charter and an unequivocal cessation of hostilities, and because the balance sought in the original draft was excluded.","locator":"Mexico statement and France/Mexico negotiation references","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous UN meeting record with explicit Mexico explanation of its position.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Mexico's UN delegation under AMLO; this is institutional diplomacy, not a personal military-order decision.","contrary_evidence":["Mexico abstained on the Russian alternative rather than backing a hard break with Russia.","The draft remained humanitarian, not a full peace settlement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Humanitarian consequences of the aggression against Ukraine : draft resolution / Albania ... Mexico ...","publisher":"United Nations Digital Library","publication_date":"2022-03-21","url":"https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3965675?ln=en","claim":"Mexico is listed among the sponsors of the humanitarian draft resolution on Ukraine, which called for an immediate cessation of hostilities, protection of civilians, and respect for international humanitarian law.","locator":"Authors list and resolution title in the record","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN depositary record directly identifies the co-sponsors and the draft text's subject.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional Mexican sponsorship under AMLO; the text shows state diplomacy rather than AMLO personally drafting it.","contrary_evidence":["Sponsorship does not prove the resolution changed the war.","This is a procedural record, so the substantive detail is limited to the title and sponsor list."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Versión estenográfica de la conferencia de prensa matutina del presidente Andrés Manuel López Obrador del 8 de septiembre de 2022","publisher":"Presidencia de la República","publication_date":"2022-09-08","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/08-09-22-version-estenografica-de-la-conferencia-de-prensa-matutina-del-presidente-andres-manuel-lopez-obrador/","claim":"AMLO said the war in Ukraine should have been avoided, said he did not agree with sanctions, and argued the goal should be to stop the war because it harms most peoples.","locator":"Lines 367-382 in the transcript","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential transcript with direct quoted statements from AMLO.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Direct AMLO attribution.","contrary_evidence":["His criticism of sanctions makes the position more pacific than aligned with coercive anti-aggression policy.","The statement is rhetorical unless tied to subsequent diplomacy."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.6","2B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Versión estenográfica de la conferencia de prensa matutina del presidente Andrés Manuel López Obrador del 12 de septiembre de 2022","publisher":"Presidencia de la República","publication_date":"2022-09-12","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/12-09-22-version-estenografica-de-la-conferencia-de-prensa-matutina-del-presidente-andres-manuel-lopez-obrador/","claim":"AMLO proposed a mediation committee with Narendra Modi, Pope Francis, and the UN Secretary-General to start talks with the presidents of Ukraine and Russia and sought a five-year truce without military exercises, nuclear practices, missiles, interventions, or internal conflict involvement.","locator":"Lines 327-328 in the transcript","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential transcript with a precise, dated peace initiative.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Direct AMLO attribution.","contrary_evidence":["Ukraine later opposed the plan as too favorable to Russia, according to independent reporting.","A proposal is not the same as an implemented ceasefire."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico foreign minister meets Russia's Lavrov to discuss Ukraine peace plan","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-24","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/24/mexico-russia-war","claim":"Reuters reported that Mexican Foreign Minister Marcelo Ebrard met Sergei Lavrov to discuss Mexico's peace plan for Ukraine, which Mexico had presented at the UN General Assembly; Ukraine opposed the plan as advantageous to Russia.","locator":"Lines 658-670 in the article","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting via Euronews is strong independent confirmation of the diplomatic initiative and the main objection to it.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Mexico's foreign minister and government under AMLO; this is state diplomacy, not a private initiative.","contrary_evidence":["Ukraine's objection is material and suggests the plan was contested.","The article does not show the plan had any concrete effect."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Fails to Adopt Resolution Condemning Moscow's Referenda in Ukraine’s Occupied Territories, as Permanent Member Employs Veto","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-09-30","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc15046.doc.htm","claim":"Mexico said it supported Ukraine's sovereignty and territorial integrity within its internationally recognized borders and voted in favor of the resolution condemning the referenda and annexation efforts.","locator":"Mexico statement in meeting coverage","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous UN record explicitly notes Mexico's vote and stated rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Mexico's Security Council vote under AMLO; institutional foreign policy rather than personal operational control.","contrary_evidence":["This is a condemnation vote, not a ceasefire success.","It shows alignment with lawful order more than direct conflict management."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Adopts Text to Suspend Russian Federation from Human Rights Council, Continuing Emergency Special Session on Humanitarian Crisis in Ukraine","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-04-07","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12414.doc.htm","claim":"Mexico said it would abstain from the draft suspending Russia from the Human Rights Council because it wanted all channels maintained for dialogue even in wartime.","locator":"Mexico statement in meeting coverage","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous UN record quoting Mexico's explanation for abstention.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Mexican delegation under AMLO; this is a policy choice at the UN, not a personal command decision.","contrary_evidence":["Abstention can be read as preserving dialogue or as reluctance to isolate an aggressor.","It is not a settlement mechanism by itself."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico, France and the UN humanitarian resolution on Ukraine","publisher":"La Jornada / AP","publication_date":"2022-03-25","url":"https://www.jornada.com.mx/noticia/2022/03/25/mundo/aprueba-onu-propuesta-humanitaria-de-mexico-y-francia-para-ucrania-2646","claim":"The AP-reported piece said the Mexico-France humanitarian resolution called for an immediate cessation of hostilities, protection of civilians, and respect for international humanitarian law, and that it passed in the General Assembly.","locator":"Lead paragraph and quoted summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"AP-reported local-language coverage corroborates the UN and Mexican-government records with an independent news frame.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional Mexican diplomacy under AMLO.","contrary_evidence":["This is still a humanitarian framework, not a negotiated peace settlement.","The article is derivative of AP reporting rather than an original investigation."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I considered roughly 30 distinct documents across the core evidence families:
- 4 UN Security Council meeting records on Ukraine from January, February, March, and September 2022.
- 4 UN General Assembly / UN Human Rights Council records on Ukraine from March, April, and November 2022.
- 6 gob.mx / SRE releases and AMLO transcript pages on Ukraine, evacuations, sanctions, and the peace proposal.
- 2 Reuters-origin reports via Euronews on the peace plan and Lavrov meeting.
- 2 local-language media pieces on the France-Mexico humanitarian draft.
- Several later 2024 retrospectives that referenced the 2022 initiative but were not necessary once the primary 2022 record was in hand.

I rejected or downweighted documents that were:
- duplicates in English/Spanish of the same government release,
- later retrospectives that merely restated 2022 events,
- out-of-scope for Chapter 2B because they were about domestic policy rather than external conduct,
- or too general to add anything beyond the local prior and the official UN record.

The main weak/blocked items were some gob.mx pages and UN digital-library pages that were hard to open directly, but their search snippets were still usable for narrow sponsor-list or headline-level claims. I did not rely on any page where I could not identify a distinct material claim.

**Remaining Gaps**
- There is still no evidence that Mexico had any military intervention, proxy war, or cross-border coercive operation in 2022. That is a real exposure gap, not a missing fact to paper over.
- I did not find evidence that AMLO's peace committee produced an actual ceasefire, negotiation track, or formal settlement in 2022.
- I did not find a meaningful contrary record of Mexican aggression, prolongation of war, or unlawful civilian harm. That is consistent with the limited-exposure profile, but it also means the chapter is judged mostly on diplomacy and restraint rather than battlefield conduct.
- If you want more depth, the only search area likely to add material value is follow-through on the September 2022 peace initiative, especially any documented UN, Russian, Ukrainian, or third-party reaction after 2022.
